{{- /*
  The layout every surface shares.

  IT CITES THE BINDING DOCUMENTS RATHER THAN PARAPHRASING THEM. The visual
  language is docs/ui-references.md, Family C, "The industrial palette", and
  ROADMAP.md step 3: a fixed bar across the top, a main column whose content is
  capped and centred, angular cards at the 0.25rem radius, system fonts only. The
  compositional reference is Cloudflare Radar — docs/ui-references.md, "The
  maintainer's recorded preferences", the General layout row — which is a left
  navigation rail, a scoped header carrying the selectors, and angular cards.
  THERE IS NO RAIL HERE, and that is a decision rather than an omission: a rail
  navigates between canvases and this cycle ships no canvases. The rail arrives
  with them, in step 7.

  WHAT THE BAR DOES CARRY IS A LINK PER SURFACE A SIGNED-IN READER MAY REACH, and
  that arrived with the second one: a route reachable only by typing its path is a
  route nobody finds, and ROADMAP.md step 7 refuses a view reachable only through a
  menu inside a menu. Links are not yet tabs, and tabs over named canvases are
  step 7's; the links are what these surfaces need in order to be reachable at all.
  The link of the page being read carries aria-current, so the bar says where the
  reader is.

  THE OUTAGE INDICATOR IS IN THE BAR OF EVERY SIGNED-IN PAGE, and links to Sources:
  the count of current outages by the rule in sources.go, or a named state of its
  own at nought. A nought would read as "we looked and nothing is wrong" in the same
  form as "three things are wrong", which is why it is a different text and not the
  same text with a different figure.

  NO BARE TEXT EXISTS IN THIS FILE OR IN ANY OTHER TEMPLATE. Every text node is a
  catalogue lookup, and a test strips the tags and the actions and fails if
  anything but whitespace is left. That is ROADMAP.md step 7's "no user-visible
  string is a literal", enforced rather than intended.

  NO EXPLANATORY COPY EITHER. A title names, a label names its field, a state is
  named in a word. Nothing here explains the product, and neither of the two
  standing limitations — the observation point, and what the key file does and does
  not protect — is recited anywhere on screen. Both are documented, in README.md.

  NOTHING IS LOADED FROM OFF-HOST. One stylesheet, served by this binary from its
  own embedded copy. No font, no script, no icon set, no favicon, no analytics.
*/ -}}
{{define "layout" -}}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{.Language}}"{{with .ThemeAttribute}} data-theme="{{.}}"{{end}}>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>{{t .TitleKey}}</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{.StylesheetPath}}">
</head>
<body>
<header class="top-bar">
<span class="product">{{t "app.name"}}</span>
{{- if .SignedIn}}
<nav class="bar-nav">
<a href="{{.SettingsPath}}"{{if eq .Surface "surface-settings"}} aria-current="page"{{end}}>{{t "settings.title"}}</a>
<a href="{{.CollectionPath}}"{{if eq .Surface "surface-collection"}} aria-current="page"{{end}}>{{t "collection.title"}}</a>
<a href="{{.InterfacesPath}}"{{if eq .Surface "surface-interfaces"}} aria-current="page"{{end}}>{{t "interfaces.title"}}</a>
<a href="{{.SourcesPath}}"{{if eq .Surface "surface-sources"}} aria-current="page"{{end}}>{{t "sources.title"}}</a>
</nav>
{{- if .OutageUnknown}}
<a class="outages outage-unknown" href="{{.SourcesPath}}"><span>{{t "indicator.unknown"}}</span></a>
{{- else if .HasOutages}}
<a class="outages has-outages" href="{{.SourcesPath}}"><span>{{t "indicator.outages"}}</span> <span class="figure">{{.OutageCount}}</span></a>
{{- else}}
<a class="outages" href="{{.SourcesPath}}"><span>{{t "indicator.no_outage"}}</span></a>
{{- end}}
<form method="post" action="{{.SignOutPath}}" class="bar-action">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
<button type="submit" class="secondary">{{t "action.sign_out"}}</button>
</form>
{{- end}}
</header>
<main class="column {{.Surface}}">
{{- if not .SettingsCard}}
{{- with .Notice}}
<p class="notice ok">{{t .}}</p>
{{- end}}
{{- with .Error}}
<p class="notice bad">{{t .}}</p>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- template "body" .}}
</main>
</body>
</html>
{{- end}}

{{- /*
  THE PIECES EVERY SURFACE DRAWS ALIKE.

  "duration" spells a length of time as its figures, each beside its unit from the
  catalogue: 1 day 2 hours. A figure is data and a unit is a string, and each is its
  own node, so neither is ever a literal.

  "figure-value" is a labelled value's value: a named state, a duration, or a figure.

  "setting-field" is one setting's field, the same on the collection surface and on
  the settings surface: a select, a figure beside its unit, or a plain figure; the
  refusal against it when there is one; and the value in force beneath it, drawn
  only when the field shows something else or when what is in force is a named
  state. A setting is therefore shown once, in its field, in the ordinary case.
*/ -}}
{{define "duration"}}{{range $index, $part := .}}{{if $index}} {{end}}<span class="duration-part"><span class="figure">{{$part.Figure}}</span> {{t $part.UnitKey}}</span>{{end}}{{end}}

{{- define "figure-value"}}{{if .StateKey}}{{t .StateKey}}{{else if .Duration}}{{template "duration" .Duration}}{{else}}<span class="figure">{{.Value}}</span>{{end}}{{end}}

{{- define "in-force-value"}}{{if .StateKey}}<span class="state">{{t .StateKey}}</span>{{else if .Parts}}{{template "duration" .Parts}}{{else}}<span class="figure">{{.Value}}</span>{{end}}{{end}}

{{- define "setting-field"}}
<div class="field{{if .RefusalKey}} invalid{{end}}">
<label for="{{.ID}}">{{t .LabelKey}}</label>
{{- if .Options}}
<select id="{{.ID}}" name="{{.Name}}"{{if .RefusalKey}} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{.ID}}_refusal" autofocus{{end}}>
{{- range .Options}}
<option value="{{.Value}}"{{if .Selected}} selected{{end}}>{{t .LabelKey}}</option>
{{- end}}
</select>
{{- else if .Units}}
<div class="duration-input">
<input id="{{.ID}}" name="{{.Name}}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="{{.Value}}"{{if .RefusalKey}} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{.ID}}_refusal" autofocus{{end}}>
<select id="{{.ID}}_unit" name="{{.UnitName}}" aria-labelledby="{{.ID}}_label_unit">
{{- range .Units}}
<option value="{{.Value}}"{{if .Selected}} selected{{end}}>{{t .LabelKey}}</option>
{{- end}}
</select>
<span class="visually-hidden" id="{{.ID}}_label_unit">{{t "field.unit"}}</span>
</div>
{{- else}}
<input id="{{.ID}}" name="{{.Name}}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="{{.Value}}"{{if .RefusalKey}} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{.ID}}_refusal" autofocus{{end}}>
{{- end}}
{{- if .RefusalKey}}
<p class="field-refusal" id="{{.ID}}_refusal">{{t .RefusalKey}}{{with .Range}} <span class="accepted-range">{{t "range.accepted_from"}} {{template "in-force-value" .Low}} {{t "range.to"}} {{template "in-force-value" .High}}</span>{{end}}</p>
{{- end}}
{{- if .ShowInForce}}
<p class="in-force"><span class="label">{{t "collection.group.in_force"}}</span> <span class="in-force-value">{{template "in-force-value" .InForce}}</span></p>
{{- end}}
</div>
{{- end}}
